Z||000004||FieroLT1||06-06-2001||08:05 AM||||Yes, it is very nice but, I'f you guys want to get back on topic here I have some "VERY" unscientific numbers I got from my own testing. By unscientific I mean stop watch and highway signs. But at least will give you and idea.<P>0-60 in 4.1secs.<BR>1/4mi in 12.5secs @ 115mph<P>Now for the unscientific:<BR>0-60 timed with a stopwatch in my left hand and shifting with the right while looking at the speedo. "VERY" dangerous in rush hour traffic.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>1/4 time starting right in front of a HWY sign that said next exit 1/4mi to so and so, to the actual exit.<P>I have not had the chance to take it to the track yet. But I will be doing that soon I hope. Also I will have it Dynoed and post the results here.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Winston Ojeda<BR><B>88 Formula LT1</B><BR>Milwaukee, Wisconsin, USA<BR><A HREF="http://www.FieroLT1.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.FieroLT1.com</A><BR><I>Home of the Fiero LT1</I><BR>  <A HREF="mailto:wojeda@FieroLT1.com">wojeda@FieroLT1.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Formula88||06-06-2001||10:08 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by FieroLT1:<BR><B>Yes, it is very nice but, I'f you guys want to get back on topic here I have some "VERY" unscientific numbers I got from my own testing. By unscientific I mean stop watch and highway signs. But at least will give you and idea.<P>0-60 in 4.1secs.<BR>1/4mi in 12.5secs @ 115mph<P>Now for the unscientific:<BR>0-60 timed with a stopwatch in my left hand and shifting with the right while looking at the speedo. "VERY" dangerous in rush hour traffic.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>1/4 time starting right in front of a HWY sign that said next exit 1/4mi to so and so, to the actual exit.<P>I have not had the chance to take it to the track yet. But I will be doing that soon I hope. Also I will have it Dynoed and post the results here.<P><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Well, your stopwatch 0-60 may be fairly good, depending on your reflexes, but the highway signs are no where near accurate enough to just 1/4 mile times with.<BR>||||reg||1
